# Archive boundary (owner, 2026-08-01): GitHub release source zips are built
# with `git archive` semantics, and Zenodo's webhook archives that zip under a
# citable DOI. The PRINCIPLE: the archive carries what a data CONSUMER needs;
# the repo carries what a CONTRIBUTOR needs. Internal working documents —
# the session coordination log, work ledgers, program docs — stay on GitHub
# and stay OUT of every published dataset artifact (Zenodo, HuggingFace,
# release downloads). If you add a new internal doc, add it here in the same
# commit. Kept in the archive deliberately: README, LICENSE, CITATION.cff,
# SCHEMA/NAMING/DECISIONS/SOURCES (they document the data itself), QUALITY.md
# (the published quality claim), ATTRIBUTION, CHANGELOG, VERSION, manifest,
# catalog/, dist/, plates/, overrides/ (curation provenance with cited
# reasons), llms.txt.

NEGOTIATION.md            export-ignore
DEBT.md                   export-ignore
AGENTS.md                 export-ignore
OWNERSHIP.yml             export-ignore
OVERNIGHT-*.md            export-ignore
CORRECTION-PASS-*.md      export-ignore
PRD-*.md                  export-ignore
PROPOSAL-*.md             export-ignore
RELEASE-DIFF-*            export-ignore
data/                     export-ignore
scripts/                  export-ignore
.github/                  export-ignore
.gitattributes            export-ignore
.gitignore                export-ignore
.aux/                     export-ignore
.claude/                  export-ignore
.ruby-lsp/                export-ignore
